# Normalise everything to LF in the repository.
#
# This tree is built on Linux CI (ubuntu-24.04) and its entry points are bash
# scripts (setup_env.sh, build_active_devices.sh). A CRLF checkout turns
# "bash ./setup_env.sh" into a hard failure, and EDK2's build tooling is
# equally unhappy about \r in .dsc/.fdf/.inc. Windows checkouts still get CRLF
# in the working tree via core.autocrlf, but the objects stay LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads - never touch these.
*.dtb binary
*.fd  binary
*.bin binary
*.img binary
*.gz  binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
*.efi binary

# Patches must be stored byte-exact: their context lines carry the CRLF
# endings of the target files inside submodules, and eol=lf normalisation
# silently breaks git apply.
*.patch -text
